{
    "_notes": "MEMSIC MXC400xXC (e.g. MXC4005XC) 3-axis accelerometer; the x in the part code sets the I2C address, 0x10-0x17. Detection: register 0x0E (device ID, 0x02 in the datasheet; 0x03 also seen). Init: 0x01 = 0x10 is INT_CLR1 with SW_RST set (a soft reset), 5 ms; 0x0D (CONTROL) = 0, +/-2 g, powered on. Poll: 7 bytes from 0x03 (XOUT, YOUT, ZOUT, 12 bits left-justified, and TOUT)",
    "addresses": "0x10-0x17",
    "detectionValues": "0x0E=0x02,0x03",
    "initValues": "0x0110=p5&0x0d00=",
    "pollInfo": {
        "c": "0x03=r7",
        "i": 100,
        "s": 3
    },
    "scanPriority": "high",
    "hwProbeEffects": {"rsao": {"effect": "none", "basis": "datasheet", "note": "MXC400xXC datasheet Rev.B: the written byte only loads the register address counter (no data byte follows, so nothing is written); no register clears on read (INT_SRC0/1 are cleared by writing INT_CLR0/1). Not documented: what the chip ACKs or returns past its 16 registers (0x00-0x0F; 0x19 is a factory register)"}},
